    {
      "id": 491894,
      "username": "UsmanSanawar",
      "name": "Usman",
      "created_at": "2026-01-20T08:02:51.478Z",
      "cooked": "<p>This is not an ERPNext issue. The Unicode symbol (U+20C1 ⃁) is saved correctly, but it is not rendering on your side because the active font on your PC / browser / PDF engine does not yet support this new glyph.</p>\n<p>Unicode support depends on font availability. On my system, a font that supports U+20C1 is available, so it displays correctly. On your system, no fallback font contains this character, so it appears missing (as in your screenshot).</p>\n<p>Possible solutions:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Update OS and browser to the latest version (newer fonts get installed automatically).</li>\n<li>Install a font that supports the symbol (e.g. Cairo, Noto Sans Arabic, Amiri).</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Once a supporting font is available, the symbol will render correctly without any ERPNext changes.</p>",
